WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
The railway reached Windermere in 1847.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.210
From the 1960s, car ownership
brought ever increasing numbers.

3
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:14.310
In 2025, 17.45 million tourists
came to the Lake District.

4
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.250
Only 38,993 people live
in the National Park.

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.510
That's about 450 tourists for
every resident, each year.

6
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:30.350
On Windermere alone, lake cruises
carried over 1.3 million people in 2022.

7
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.690
So what do all those visitors
do to this landscape?

8
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.850
Are the hills big enough for everyone?

9
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.430
In this mission, you'll sort
tourism's impacts on the economy,

10
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.190
on local people and on the land.

11
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.010
Then you'll judge the strategies
used to manage the Park,

12
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.010
and their drawbacks.

13
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.490
Your mission: find out what all those
visitors do to the Lake District.
